{"timestamp":"2026-04-09T15:22:52.641Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The calculator page now has a real lathe and wire auto-programming lane wired into the backend, not a placeholder surface. I added the shared workbench in [CalculatorProgramWorkbench.tsx](/H:/PRISM/mcp-server/web/src/components/calculator/CalculatorProgramWorkbench.tsx), the lathe API seam in [latheTurning.ts](/H:/PRISM/mcp-server/web/src/api/latheTurning.ts), and mounted it into [CalculatorPage.tsx](/H:/PRISM/mcp-server/web/src/pages/CalculatorPage.tsx). For both `lathe` and `wire_edm`, the page now gives you:\n- a print/CAD upload dropbox\n- a `PRISM auto-program` action\n- `2D` / `3D` part-view toggles\n- feature or contour selection\n- offset/allowance inputs\n- generated NC output with download actions\n- a direct handoff link into the full Print to CNC flow\n\nThe backend wiring now hits the intended live routes:\n- lathe upload and feature extraction: `/api/v1/lathe/upload`\n- lathe program generation: `/api/v1/turning/program`\n- wire geometry parse: `/api/v1/edm/parse-geometry`\n- wire auto-program: `/api/v1/edm/photo-to-program`\n\nVerification is green:\n- `npm run build` in `H:\\PRISM\\mcp-server\\web`\n- [CalculatorPage.autoProgramming.test.tsx](/H:/PRISM/mcp-server/web/src/__tests__/CalculatorPage.autoProgramming.test.tsx): `2/2`\n- [CalculatorPage.solveWorkflows.test.tsx](/H:/PRISM/mcp-server/web/src/__tests__/CalculatorPage.solveWorkflows.test.tsx): `6/6`\n- backend route checks: `lathe-turning-routes.test.ts` `14/14`, `turning-edm-routes.test.ts` `4/4`\n\nOne honest boundary remains: wire feature-by-feature selection is strongest on `DXF` uploads, because that is where the page can parse real selectable contours. Image/PDF uploads still auto-program, but they do not yet unlock the same contour-selection fidelity unless geometry is available.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
