surfaces. Toolpath classification is clean: `337` toolpaths audited, `0` left in an uncategorized general bucket, and the live-tool / Swiss split is explicitly covered in [calculatorCatalogCoverage.test.ts](/H:/PRISM/mcp-server/web/src/__tests__/calculatorCatalogCoverage.test.ts#L693). Machine-profile source coverage is broad: the source catalogs contain `1,941` machine profiles across `49` brands, and the normalization/major-brand checks are covered in [machineConfigurationOptions.test.ts](/H:/PRISM/mcp-server/web/src/__tests__/machineConfigurationOptions.test.ts#L120) and [machineConfigurationOptions.test.ts](/H:/PRISM/mcp-server/web/src/__tests__/machineConfigurationOptions.test.ts#L151).\n\nVerification today, April 6, 2026:\n- Web calculator sweep: `152/152` passing in `H:\\PRISM\\mcp-server\\web`\n- CAD/CAM + post + real-part pipeline sweep: `675/675` passing in `H:\\PRISM\\mcp-server`\n- Full WEDM/CWEDM family: `1478/1478` passing in `H:\\PRISM\\mcp-server`\n\nThat’s `2305/2305` passing across the main comprehensive batches, including the matrix tests that exercise thousands of machine/material/tooling/toolpath combinations.\n\nOne honest caveat remains: the web picker itself is still a curated subset of the much larger machine-profile catalogs. The coverage and normalization are there, but if you want every supported profile surfaced directly in the calculator UI, that’s a separate expansion rather than a bugfix."}],"phase":"final_answer"},{"type":"message","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"we need full access and full wiring of our databases to the intended calculator page feature so we can comprehensively test\n"}]},{"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The calculator is now wired more like the intended live product path instead of a partly bundled demo path. I added a backend programming catalog route in [data.ts](/H:/PRISM/mcp-server/src/routes/data.ts#L93), taught the calculator data layer to l