49), [CalculatorPage.solveWorkflows.test.tsx](/H:/PRISM/mcp-server/web/src/__tests__/CalculatorPage.solveWorkflows.test.tsx#L288), [CalculatorPage.solveWorkflows.test.tsx](/H:/PRISM/mcp-server/web/src/__tests__/CalculatorPage.solveWorkflows.test.tsx#L329), and [CalculatorPage.solveWorkflows.test.tsx](/H:/PRISM/mcp-server/web/src/__tests__/CalculatorPage.solveWorkflows.test.tsx#L381). Those now walk full UI solves for:\n- 3-axis steel roughing\n- 5-axis swarf finishing\n- conventional VTL rough turning\n- Swiss synchronized turning\n- live-tool mill-turn\n- wire EDM skim finishing\n\nVerification is green:\n- Web calculator/comprehensive batch: `98/98` passing in `H:\\PRISM\\mcp-server\\web`\n- Backend CAD/CAM + WEDM batch: `381/381` passing in `H:\\PRISM\\mcp-server`\n- Total post-fix reruns: `479/479` passing\n\nThose passing batches include the large matrix sweeps and max-variability coverage in [calculatorCatalogCoverage.test.ts](/H:/PRISM/mcp-server/web/src/__tests__/calculatorCatalogCoverage.test.ts#L573), [calculatorCatalogCoverage.test.ts](/H:/PRISM/mcp-server/web/src/__tests__/calculatorCatalogCoverage.test.ts#L693), and [calculatorCatalogCoverage.test.ts](/H:/PRISM/mcp-server/web/src/__tests__/calculatorCatalogCoverage.test.ts#L722), which exercise thousands of logical machine/material/toolpath/tooling combinations plus the new machine-aware live-tool/Swiss guardrails.\n\nOne honest remaining limitation: the calculator still is not a pure raw-database browser everywhere. Workholding is still curated in-page, and materials/tools still merge live data with curated fallback. So the feature is now much more comprehensively testable, but those two surfaces can still mask a backend completeness gap if one appears."}],"phase":"final_answer"},{"type":"message","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Lauch agents for all machine types, continue running tests. make sure all models from all major suppliers are tested thoroughly.\n"}]},{"type":"message","