{"timestamp":"2026-04-09T15:24:02.040Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"exec_command_end","call_id":"call_EXPl73TLES1HXwPWgtaPhqpu","turn_id":"019d72d6-ccb9-7092-9a54-07afc93f2ff7","command":["C:\\Program Files\\PowerShell\\7\\pwsh.exe","-Command","Get-Content -LiteralPath 'H:\\PRISM\\state\\shared\\TASK_COORDINATION_SPEC.md' -TotalCount 220"],"cwd":"H:\\","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'H:\\PRISM\\state\\shared\\TASK_COORDINATION_SPEC.md' -TotalCount 220"}],"source":"agent","stdout":"","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# Task Coordination System Spec\r\n## Claude + Codex Shared Job Queue\r\n\r\nGenerated: 2026-03-28T03:30:00Z\r\nStatus: DRAFT — both agents should review and adopt\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\nThe coordination system has a solid awareness layer (workboard, chat, directives) but\r\nlacks automatic job assignment. A new terminal cannot automatically pick the next\r\navailable task, check if its dependencies are met, or know if another terminal already\r\nclaimed it.\r\n\r\n## Design Goals\r\n\r\n1. **File-based** — JSON + MD so both Claude and Codex can read/write\r\n2. **Identity-aware** — uses existing `agent-identity.mjs` for claim ownership\r\n3. **Dependency-ordered** — tasks have `blocked_by` fields pointing to prerequisite tasks\r\n4. **Claim-locked** — only one instance can work a task at a time\r\n5. **Heartbeat-expiring** — stale claims auto-reap after 10 minutes with no heartbeat\r\n6. **Family-filtered** — Claude sees backend tasks, Codex sees frontend tasks\r\n7. **Workboard-integrated** — claiming/completing updates the workboard automatically\r\n\r\n## Shared Files\r\n\r\n| File | Purpose |\r\n|------|---------|\r\n| `state/shared/TASK_QUEUE.json` | Machine-readable task queue |\r\n| `state/shared/TASK_QUEUE.md` | Human-readable task board |\r\n| `.claude/helpers/task-queue.mjs` | CLI helper both agents call |\r\n\r\n## Task Schema\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"id\": \"C1-SHELL-BOOTSTRAP\",\r\n  \"title\": \"Create ShellBootstrapEngine\",\r\n  \"sprint\": \"C1\",\r\n  \"owner_family\": \"Claude\",\r\n  \"status\": \"available\",\r\n  \"blocked_by\": [],\r\n  \"claimed_by\": null,\r\n  \"claimed_at\": null,\r\n  \"heartbeat_at\": null,\r\n  \"completed_at\": null,\r\n  \"completed_by\": null,\r\n  \"priority\": 1,\r\n  \"estimated_loc\": 200,\r\n  \"files\": [\"src/engines/ShellBootstrapEngine.ts\"],\r\n  \"description\": \"Shell navigation + role profiles\",\r\n  \"notes\": \"\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Task Lifecycle\r\n\r\n```\r\navailable ──claim──> claimed ──start──> in_progress ──complete──> completed\r\n    ^                   |                    |\r\n    |                   v                    v\r\n    +────release────────+────heartbeat───────+\r\n    |                                        |\r\n    +────────────reap (stale > 10min)────────+\r\n```\r\n\r\nStatus values: `available`, `claimed`, `in_progress`, `completed`, `blocked`\r\n\r\n- `blocked` = auto-computed: if any `blocked_by` task is not `completed`, status = `blocked`\r\n- When a blocking task completes, downstream tasks auto-transition from `blocked` → `available`\r\n\r\n## CLI Commands\r\n\r\nAll commands auto-detect identity via `agent-identity.mjs`.\r\n\r\n| Command | Description |\r\n|---------|-------------|\r\n| `task-queue.mjs list` | Show all tasks grouped by status |\r\n| `task-queue.mjs next` | Find highest-priority unblocked task for your family |\r\n| `task-queue.mjs claim --task <id>` | Claim a task (sets claimed_by + timestamp) |\r\n| `task-queue.mjs start --task <id>` | Mark in_progress (updates workboard) |\r\n| `task-queue.mjs heartbeat --task <id>` | Refresh heartbeat timestamp |\r\n| `task-queue.mjs complete --task <id>` | Mark completed (updates workboard, unblocks dependents) |\r\n| `task-queue.mjs release --task <id>` | Release a claim back to available |\r\n| `task-queue.mjs reap` | Reclaim all stale tasks (heartbeat > 10 min) |\r\n| `task-queue.mjs add --task <json>` | Add a new task to the queue |\r\n\r\n## Integration Points\r\n\r\n### On `/startup`\r\n1. Read TASK_QUEUE.json\r\n2. Run `reap` to clear stale claims\r\n3. Run `next` to suggest the top available task\r\n4. Display available task count in startup summary\r\n\r\n### On work start\r\n1. `claim --task <id>` → locks the task\r\n2. `start --task <id>` → updates workboard with current/next\r\n3. Heartbeat hook runs every 2 min to keep claim alive\r\n\r\n### On `/compact`\r\n1. `heartbeat --task <id>` → refresh before compaction\r\n2. `task-queue.mjs compact-sync` → refresh active claim heartbeats and auto-complete any probe-verifiable finished tasks\r\n3. Completed task ids/titles are written into shared roadmap sync `done` state for compact-aware recovery\r\n4. Task ID saved in HANDOFF.md → RESUME section references it\r\n\r\n### On work complete\r\n1. `complete --task <id>` → marks done, unblocks dependents\r\n2. Posts to AGENT_CHAT\r\n3. Updates workboard with completion + next available\r\n\r\n## Ownership Rules\r\n\r\n- `owner_family: \"Claude\"` = backend tasks (engines, routes, dispatchers, physics)\r\n- `owner_family: \"Codex\"` = frontend tasks (pages, providers, components, hooks)\r\n- `owner_family: \"any\"` = either agent can claim (audits, reviews, convergence checks)\r\n- A task can ONLY be claimed by its owner family (enforced by CLI)\r\n\r\n## Dependency Examples\r\n\r\n```\r\nC1-ROUTES blocked_by: [C1-SHELL-BOOTSTRAP, C1-JOB-DESK, C1-PROGRAM-RELEASE, C1-SCHEDULING, C1-SHOP-FLOOR]\r\nF1-SWAP-FIXTURES blocked_by: [C1-ROUTES]  (Codex blocked until Claude lands C1)\r\nC2-WIRE-PAGES blocked_by: [C1-ROUTES]\r\nF2-IMPLEMENT-STUBS blocked_by: [C2-WIRE-PAGES]\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Adoption\r\n\r\n- **Claude**: Use `task-queue.mjs` via Bash tool in sessions. Wire into `/startup` and `/compact`.\r\n- **Codex**: Use `task-queue.mjs` via shell execution. Wire into startup and session lifecycle.\r\n- **Both**: Read TASK_QUEUE.md for human-readable board. Post completions to AGENT_CHAT.\r\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":669084400},"formatted_output":"","status":"completed"}}
